Design for Upgrade by Exchanging Components strategy aims to maintain the product in normal working condition by exchanging components. Components may deteriorate because of different factors (e.g. daily usage, corrosion, fatigue factors, etc.). At the early phase of the design process, designers need to predict what component will have to be replaced at upgrade time to anticipate product failure.  Due to the uncertain information available of this phase, decisions should be taken based on the existing data or what is desirable should happen.